module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjLargeDegreeSections.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistSectionRing.Statement

/-!
# The kernel half of Tag 0AG7 for the regular module, discharged

`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjLargeDegreeSections.exists_bijective_degreeNToGlobalSections` is
[Stacks, Tag 0AG7] — the canonical maps `M_n ⟶ Γ(Proj 𝒮, M(n)~)` of Equation 01MR are bijective
in all large degrees — with the source's hypotheses "`𝒮 0` Noetherian" and "`M` finite" replaced
by homogeneous generating data for the *kernel* and for the *cokernel* of the comparison. This
file discharges the kernel half of that data, for `M = S` the graded ring itself, out of
`IsNoetherianRing S` and generation in degree one, which is how the source gets it.

The kernel is identified by `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/ProjSaturation/Basic.lean`: the
canonical section `degreeSection 𝒮 n b` of `𝒪(n)` attached to `b ∈ 𝒮 n` vanishes exactly when a
power of the irrelevant ideal annihilates `b`. So the homogeneous elements of the kernel are the
`𝒮₊`-power torsion ones, the ideal they generate is finitely generated because `S` is Noetherian,
and finitely many of them generate it — which is the data `x`, `dx`, `Nx`, `hxtors`, `hxgen`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjLargeDegreeSections.homogeneousVanishing`: the set of
  homogeneous elements of `S` whose canonical twisted global section vanishes.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjLargeDegreeSections.degreeNToGlobalSections_eq_zero_iff`: for the
  regular grading the canonical map of Equation 01MR *is* the canonical twisted section of
  [Stacks, Tag 01MP], so its kernel is the one `ProjSaturation` computes.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjLargeDegreeSections.exists_homogeneous_generators`: finitely many
  homogeneous elements of the kernel generate every homogeneous element of it.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjLargeDegreeSections.exists_homogeneous_coeffs`: a homogeneous
  element of the ideal generated by homogeneous `x j` of degrees `d j` is a combination of the
  `x j` with homogeneous coefficients of the complementary degrees.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjLargeDegreeSections`
  `.exists_bijective_degreeNToGlobalSections_regular`: **[Stacks, Tag 0AG7] for the regular
  module with only the cokernel data assumed.**

## Implementation notes

The regular module of `S`, graded over `ℤ`, is
`AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.integerGrading 𝒮` — the nonnegative grading extended
by `⊥` in negative degrees, which is the family the twisting sheaves are built from. That it is a
graded module over `𝒮` is the instance `integerGradingGradedSMul` below; only the shifts
`twistGrading 𝒮 n` carried one before, and `twistGrading 𝒮 0` is not that family on the nose.

With that in place `degreeNToGlobalSections 𝒮 (integerGrading 𝒮) (n : ℕ)` and `degreeSection 𝒮 n`
are *the same map*: both are the degree-zero global-sections map of [Stacks, Tag 01M7] applied to
the shift of the regular module, so the identification is `rfl` and no comparison isomorphism
intervenes.

The passage from "finitely generated ideal" to "finitely many *homogeneous* generators" does not
go through homogeneity of the kernel ideal: the ideal generated by the homogeneous vanishing
elements is finitely generated, each of its finitely many generators lies in the span of a finite
subset of the vanishing set (`Submodule.mem_span_finite_of_mem_span`), and the union of those
subsets is the homogeneous generating family. Nothing has to be said about the components of a
non-homogeneous element of the kernel.

`exists_homogeneous_coeffs` takes the coefficient degrees as a family `e` with `e j + d j = k`
rather than forming `k - d j`, so that `DirectSum.coe_decompose_mul_add_of_right_mem` applies
with no index cast; the consumer instantiates `e` at the `(n - dx j).toNat` the general statement
asks for.

**No `@[stacks 0AG7]` attribute is attached here.** The tag's site is
`exists_bijective_degreeNToGlobalSections` in `ProjLargeDegreeSections/Basic.lean`, and that
site's attribute describes a statement assuming both halves of the data. What this file means is
that the kernel half of that description is dischargeable, for `M = S`; the cokernel half is not,
and needs [Stacks, Tag 0AG6] clause (4) = [Stacks, Tag 01YS] clause (5). That clause is proved
for projective space:
`Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.Cohomology.moduleFinite_truncation_of_isCoherent` in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/ProjectiveSpace/Cohomology/TwistSectionsDegreeOne.lean`. What it
is not available for is a *general* `Proj 𝒮`, which is the generality this file's statements are
in — so the cokernel half is out of reach here, not out of reach everywhere.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AG7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AG7)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01MP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01MP)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BXD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BXD)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open DirectSum AlgebraicGeometry AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjShiftedSections
  (shiftedSectionsComponent degreeNToGlobalSections homogeneousScalarGlobalSections)
open scoped Stacks.GradedLocalization

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjLargeDegreeSections

universe u w

variable {S : Type u} {σ : Type w} [CommRing S] [SetLike σ S] [AddSubgroupClass σ S]
  (𝒮 : ℕ → σ) [GradedRing 𝒮]

/-! ### The regular module as a `ℤ`-graded module -/

/-- **The regular module of a nonnegatively graded ring is a `ℤ`-graded module over it**, for the
grading extended by `⊥` in negative degrees: a homogeneous scalar of degree `i` carries the
degree-`j` piece into the degree-`i + j` piece, the negative pieces being trivial. -/
instance integerGradingGradedSMul :
    SetLike.GradedSMul 𝒮 (integerGrading (S := S) 𝒮) where
  smul_mem := by
    intro i j a b ha hb
    rcases lt_or_ge j 0 with hj | hj
    · have hb0 : b ∈ (⊥ : Submodule ℤ S) := by
        simpa [integerGrading, not_le.mpr hj] using hb
      have hbz : b = 0 := by simpa using hb0
      subst hbz
      rw [smul_zero]
      exact zero_mem _
    · have hb' : b ∈ 𝒮 j.toNat := by
        simpa [integerGrading, hj, homogeneousSubmodule] using hb
      have hnn : (0 : ℤ) ≤ (i : ℤ) + j := by omega
      have heq : ((i : ℤ) + j).toNat = i + j.toNat := by omega
      have hmul : a * b ∈ 𝒮 (i + j.toNat) := SetLike.mul_mem_graded ha hb'
      change a • b ∈ integerGrading (S := S) 𝒮 ((i : ℤ) + j)
      simpa [integerGrading, hnn, heq, homogeneousSubmodule, smul_eq_mul] using hmul

/-- For the regular module the canonical map `S_n ⟶ Γ(Proj 𝒮, S(n)~)` of Equation 01MR is the
canonical twisted section of [Stacks, Tag 01MP]: both are the degree-zero global-sections map of
the shift `S(n)`, so the two vanish together. -/
theorem degreeNToGlobalSections_eq_zero_iff (k : ℕ) (b : 𝒮 k)
    (hb : (b : S) ∈ integerGrading (S := S) 𝒮 (k : ℤ)) :
    degreeNToGlobalSections 𝒮 (integerGrading (S := S) 𝒮) (k : ℤ) ⟨(b : S), hb⟩ = 0 ↔
      degreeSection 𝒮 k b = 0 := Iff.rfl

/-! ### The homogeneous elements of the kernel -/

/-- **The homogeneous part of the kernel of `S ⟶ ⨁_{n ≥ 0} Γ(Proj 𝒮, 𝒪(n))`**: the homogeneous
elements whose canonical twisted global section vanishes. -/
def homogeneousVanishing : Set S :=
  {b | ∃ (n : ℕ) (hb : b ∈ 𝒮 n), degreeSection 𝒮 n ⟨b, hb⟩ = 0}

/-- **Finitely many homogeneous elements of the kernel generate all of them.** The ideal they
generate is finitely generated because `S` is Noetherian, each of its generators lies in the span
of a finite subset of the homogeneous vanishing elements, and the union of those finite subsets is
the family. -/
theorem exists_homogeneous_generators [IsNoetherianRing S] :
    ∃ (r : ℕ) (x : Fin r → S) (d : Fin r → ℕ) (hx : ∀ j, x j ∈ 𝒮 (d j)),
      (∀ j, degreeSection 𝒮 (d j) ⟨x j, hx j⟩ = 0) ∧
        homogeneousVanishing 𝒮 ⊆ Ideal.span (Set.range x) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ : (Ideal.span (homogeneousVanishing 𝒮)).FG :=
    Ideal.fg_of_isNoetherianRing _
  have key : ∀ a : S, ∃ T : Finset S, (↑T : Set S) ⊆ homogeneousVanishing 𝒮 ∧
      (a ∈ Ideal.span (homogeneousVanishing 𝒮) → a ∈ Ideal.span (↑T : Set S)) := by
    intro a
    by_cases ha : a ∈ Ideal.span (homogeneousVanishing 𝒮)
    · obtain ⟨T, hTsub, hTmem⟩ := Submodule.mem_span_finite_of_mem_span ha
      exact ⟨T, hTsub, fun _ => hTmem⟩
    · exact ⟨∅, by simp, fun h => absurd h ha⟩
  choose T hT1 hT2 using key
  set U : Finset S := t.biUnion T with hU
  have hUsub : (↑U : Set S) ⊆ homogeneousVanishing 𝒮 := by
    intro a ha
    simp only [hU, Finset.coe_biUnion, Set.mem_iUnion] at ha
    obtain ⟨b, -, hab⟩ := ha
    exact hT1 b hab
  have hsubU : ∀ a ∈ t, (↑(T a) : Set S) ⊆ (↑U : Set S) := by
    intro a hat z hz
    simp only [hU, Finset.coe_biUnion, Set.mem_iUnion]
    exact ⟨a, hat, hz⟩
  have hspanU : Ideal.span (homogeneousVanishing 𝒮) ≤ Ideal.span (↑U : Set S) := by
    rw [← ht, Ideal.span_le]
    intro a hat
    refine Ideal.span_mono (hsubU a hat) (hT2 a ?_)
    rw [← ht]
    exact Submodule.subset_span hat
  refine ⟨Fintype.card (↥U), fun j => (((Fintype.equivFin (↥U)).symm j : ↥U) : S), ?_⟩
  have hmemU : ∀ j : Fin (Fintype.card (↥U)),
      (((Fintype.equivFin (↥U)).symm j : ↥U) : S) ∈ homogeneousVanishing 𝒮 :=
    fun j => hUsub ((Fintype.equivFin (↥U)).symm j).2
  choose d hd hd0 using hmemU
  refine ⟨d, hd, hd0, ?_⟩
  have hrange :
      (↑U : Set S) ⊆ Set.range fun j => (((Fintype.equivFin (↥U)).symm j : ↥U) : S) := by
    intro a ha
    exact ⟨Fintype.equivFin (↥U) ⟨a, ha⟩, by simp⟩
  intro b hb
  exact Ideal.span_mono hrange (hspanU (Submodule.subset_span hb))

/-- **Homogeneous coefficients.** A homogeneous element of degree `k` of the ideal generated by
homogeneous elements `x j` of degrees `d j` is a combination `∑ a j * x j` with each `a j`
homogeneous of the complementary degree `e j`, where `e j + d j = k`: take the degree-`k`
component of any representation. -/
theorem exists_homogeneous_coeffs {r : ℕ} (x : Fin r → S) (d e : Fin r → ℕ)
    (hx : ∀ j, x j ∈ 𝒮 (d j)) {k : ℕ} (he : ∀ j, e j + d j = k) {m : S} (hm : m ∈ 𝒮 k)
    (hmem : m ∈ Ideal.span (Set.range x)) :
    ∃ a : (j : Fin r) → 𝒮 (e j), m = ∑ j, (a j : S) * x j := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := (Submodule.mem_span_range_iff_exists_fun S).mp hmem
  refine ⟨fun j => DirectSum.decompose 𝒮 (c j) (e j), ?_⟩
  calc m = GradedRing.proj 𝒮 k m := by
        rw [GradedRing.proj_apply, DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_same 𝒮 hm]
    _ = GradedRing.proj 𝒮 k (∑ j, c j • x j) := by rw [hc]
    _ = ∑ j, GradedRing.proj 𝒮 k (c j • x j) := map_sum _ _ _
    _ = ∑ j, (DirectSum.decompose 𝒮 (c j) (e j) : S) * x j := by
        refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ => ?_
        rw [GradedRing.proj_apply, smul_eq_mul, ← he j]
        exact DirectSum.coe_decompose_mul_add_of_right_mem 𝒮 (hx j)

/-! ### Tag 0AG7 for the regular module, with only the cokernel data assumed -/

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0AG7] for the regular module `M = S`, with the kernel data discharged.** Let
`S = ⨁_{d ≥ 0} 𝒮 d` be a Noetherian graded ring generated in degree one over `𝒮 0`, and let
`X = Proj 𝒮`. If the cokernel of the comparison `S_n ⟶ Γ(X, S(n)~)` is generated degreewise by
finitely many sections `y k` which a power of the irrelevant ideal carries into the image, then
the comparison is bijective in every sufficiently large degree.

The kernel data the general statement
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjLargeDegreeSections.exists_bijective_degreeNToGlobalSections`
asks for is produced here: the homogeneous elements of the kernel are the `𝒮₊`-power torsion
ones (`AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.degreeSection_eq_zero_iff`), finitely many of
them generate the rest because `S` is Noetherian (`exists_homogeneous_generators`), and a
homogeneous element of the ideal they generate has homogeneous coefficients of the complementary
degrees (`exists_homogeneous_coeffs`). -/
theorem exists_bijective_degreeNToGlobalSections_regular [IsNoetherianRing S]
    (hgen : Algebra.adjoin (𝒮 0) (𝒮 1 : Set S) = ⊤)
    {cq : ℕ} (dy : Fin cq → ℤ) (Ny : Fin cq → ℕ)
    (y : (k : Fin cq) → shiftedSectionsComponent 𝒮 (integerGrading (S := S) 𝒮) (dy k))
    (hytors : ∀ (k : Fin cq) (i : ℕ) (a : 𝒮 i),
      (a : S) ∈ (HomogeneousIdeal.irrelevant 𝒮).toIdeal ^ Ny k →
        ∃ m : integerGrading (S := S) 𝒮 ((i : ℤ) + dy k),
          homogeneousScalarGlobalSections 𝒮 (integerGrading (S := S) 𝒮) i (dy k) a (y k)
            = degreeNToGlobalSections 𝒮 (integerGrading (S := S) 𝒮) ((i : ℤ) + dy k) m)
    (hygen : ∀ (n : ℤ) (hn : ∀ k, dy k ≤ n)
        (s : shiftedSectionsComponent 𝒮 (integerGrading (S := S) 𝒮) n),
      ∃ (m : integerGrading (S := S) 𝒮 n) (a : (k : Fin cq) → 𝒮 (n - dy k).toNat),
        s = degreeNToGlobalSections 𝒮 (integerGrading (S := S) 𝒮) n m +
          ∑ k, ofDegreeEq 𝒮 (integerGrading (S := S) 𝒮)
            (show (((n - dy k).toNat : ℤ) + dy k) = n by have := hn k; omega)
            (homogeneousScalarGlobalSections 𝒮 (integerGrading (S := S) 𝒮)
              ((n - dy k).toNat) (dy k) (a k) (y k))) :
    ∃ n₀ : ℤ, ∀ n : ℤ, n₀ ≤ n →
      Function.Bijective (degreeNToGlobalSections 𝒮 (integerGrading (S := S) 𝒮) n) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨r, x, d, hx, hx0, hspan⟩ := exists_homogeneous_generators 𝒮
  choose Nx hNx using fun j : Fin r =>
    exists_irrelevant_pow_le_annihilator_of_degreeSection_eq_zero 𝒮 hgen ⟨x j, hx j⟩ (hx0 j)
  refine exists_bijective_degreeNToGlobalSections 𝒮 (integerGrading (S := S) 𝒮) hgen
    x (fun j => (d j : ℤ)) Nx (fun j a ha => ?_) (fun n hn m hm => ?_) dy Ny y hytors hygen
  · exact (Submodule.mem_annihilator_span_singleton (x j) a).mp (hNx j ha)
  · rcases lt_or_ge n 0 with hneg | hnn
    · refine ⟨fun j => 0, ?_⟩
      have hm0 : (m : S) = 0 := by
        have hmb : (m : S) ∈ (⊥ : Submodule ℤ S) := by
          simpa [integerGrading, not_le.mpr hneg] using m.2
        simpa using hmb
      simp [hm0]
    · obtain ⟨k, rfl⟩ : ∃ k : ℕ, n = (k : ℤ) := ⟨n.toNat, (Int.toNat_of_nonneg hnn).symm⟩
      have hmk : (m : S) ∈ 𝒮 k := by
        simpa [integerGrading, homogeneousSubmodule] using m.2
      have hdk : ∀ j, d j ≤ k := fun j => by have := hn j; omega
      have hvan : degreeSection 𝒮 k ⟨(m : S), hmk⟩ = 0 :=
        (degreeNToGlobalSections_eq_zero_iff 𝒮 k ⟨(m : S), hmk⟩ m.2).mp hm
      have hmem : (m : S) ∈ Ideal.span (Set.range x) := hspan ⟨k, hmk, hvan⟩
      obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := exists_homogeneous_coeffs 𝒮 x d
        (fun j => ((k : ℤ) - (d j : ℤ)).toNat) hx
        (fun j => by have := hdk j; omega) hmk hmem
      exact ⟨a, by simpa [smul_eq_mul] using ha⟩

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjLargeDegreeSections

end
